.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt WITH-GNU-MAKE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm with-gnu-make
.Nd run a command with GNU make exposed as make
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar arg ...
.Nm
.Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs
.Ar command
with GNU make answering to the name
.Ic make ,
and the C compiler to the name
.Ic gcc
where there is no
.Ic gcc .
It is meant for Python source distributions that build a bundled C
library, which call
.Ic make
and
.Ic gcc
by those names: on
.Fx ,
.Ic make
is BSD make, which cannot read a GNU makefile, and there is no
.Ic gcc
at all, so the nested build fails, often with a warning only, the
breakage showing later as a missing
.Pa .a
or
.Pa .o
file.
.Pp
.Nm
writes shims, small scripts that run the real tool by its full path,
into a directory it puts first on
.Ev PATH ,
then replaces itself with the command, so that any build the command
starts finds them.
A shim is written only where it is needed:
.Ic make
when the
.Ic make
on
.Ev PATH
is not GNU make, as its
.Fl -version
tells,
and
.Ic gcc
when there is none.
A shim left by an earlier run that is no longer needed is removed, so
it does not shadow a
.Ic make
that has become usable.
Where both are already there, as on a GNU/Linux system with
.Ic gcc ,
the command is run unchanged.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage, with the values of the variables below, and exit.
Only the first argument is taken for an option; every other is the
command's.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width SHIM_DIR
.It Ev GNU_MAKE
The GNU make to shim in as
.Ic make ,
instead of
.Ic gmake .
.It Ev SHIM_CC
The C compiler to shim in as
.Ic gcc ,
instead of
.Ic cc .
.It Ev SHIM_DIR
The directory of the shims, instead of
.Pa ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-~/.cache}/with-gnu-make/bin .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The exit status of
.Ar command ;
1 when a shim is needed and cannot be made: no
.Ev GNU_MAKE
found, or one that is not GNU make, no
.Ev SHIM_CC
found, or a target the shim cannot name
.Pq Sx CAVEATS ;
2 for a usage error, a missing
.Ar command
included.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Install a Python package that builds LuaJIT:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ with-gnu-make uv pip install lupa
.Ed
.Pp
Run a tool whose dependencies build C code on first use:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ with-gnu-make uvx --from openhands-agent-server==1.44.0 agent-server
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cc 1 ,
.Xr gmake 1 ,
.Xr make 1
.Sh CAVEATS
A shim's target is written between single quotes, so a path holding
one is refused; so is a target inside
.Ev SHIM_DIR ,
a shim of a shim.
